# Copy this file to ".env" in the project root and fill in your keys.
#   Windows:      copy .env.example .env
#   macOS/Linux:  cp .env.example .env
# ".env" is git-ignored; never commit real keys.
#
# SEVERAL KEYS PER PLATFORM: fill in as many as you have (_1, _2, _3 ... up to _20;
# gaps are fine, empty lines are ignored). When a key is rate-limited (429), out of
# quota/credits or invalid, the pipeline switches to the next one automatically
# (experiments/api_keys.py). One key per platform also works.
#
# Gemini quotas are per Google Cloud PROJECT, not per key: keys from the same project
# share one quota, so use keys from different projects/accounts (e.g. one per team member).

# --- Gemini API: translation (step 1) and judge (step 4) ----------------------
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_API_KEY_1=
GOOGLE_API_KEY_2=
GOOGLE_API_KEY_3=

# --- Sarvam AI: text-to-speech (step 2, costs credits) ------------------------
# Sarvam dashboard -> API subscription key. Each key uses its own account's credits.
SARVAM_API_KEY_1=
SARVAM_API_KEY_2=
SARVAM_API_KEY_3=

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Legacy Groq/Orpheus TTS path only (--tts-provider groq). Not used by default.
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# Hugging Face token, only if the Gemma 4 download asks you to log in / accept a licence.
# HF_TOKEN=
